# Release Checklist

Before bumping VERSION, tagging a release, or publishing to npm, **every item below must be verified**. Do NOT skip steps. If a doc is stale, fix it before proceeding.

## 1. Documentation currency

| File | Check |
|------|-------|
| `README.md` | "What it does" list matches shipped features. Status section reflects current test count, version, and milestone. |
| `AGENTS.md` | Section 6 (Current Status) matches reality. Section 9 (What NOT to do) has no stale restrictions from completed milestones. |
| `CLAUDE.md` | "What done means" criteria are current. Anti-patterns table is not referencing completed/removed concerns. |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | `[Unreleased]` section is promoted to a dated version header matching `VERSION`. A fresh empty `[Unreleased]` section exists above it. |
| `docs/ROADMAP.md` | Completed milestone is marked ✅. Next milestone is clearly identified. |
| `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` | Architecture diagram includes all shipped components. "What's intentionally missing" list has no items that have shipped. |
| `docs/ADAPTER-SDK.md` | SDK version matches `packages/adapter-sdk/package.json`. API examples compile against current interfaces. |

## 2. Version consistency

- `VERSION` file matches the version header in `CHANGELOG.md`
- `VERSION` file matches `version` in root `package.json` (if present)
- `CHANGELOG.md` has a dated `[x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` header for the new version
- If adapter-sdk version changed, `docs/ADAPTER-SDK.md` status line is updated

## 3. Quality gates

- All tests pass: `bun test` (full suite)
- Lint is clean: `bunx biome check .`
- No `TODO` or `FIXME` comments referencing the releasing milestone

## 4. After tagging

- Push tag: `git tag v<version> && git push origin v<version>`
- Verify CI release workflow triggers
- Update `docs/ROADMAP.md` if the milestone gate includes "publish to npm"
